  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two integers NNN and KKK. Count the number of permutations†^\\dagger† PPP of the integers 111 to NNN satisfy the following condition:\n\n\nThere exists **at least one** index iii (1≤i&lt;N(1 \\leq i \\lt N(1≤i&lt;N) such that Pi+Pi+1=KP_i + P_{i+1} = KPi​+Pi+1​=K.\nSince the count can be very large, print it modulo 109+710^9+7109+7.\n\n†^\\dagger† A permutation of the integers 111 to NNN is an array of length NNN that contains every integer from 111 to NNN exactly once.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK ― the length of the permutation and the required sum.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print on a new line a single integer: the number of valid permutations, modulo 109+710^9+7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N,K≤1051 \\le N,K \\le 10^51≤N,K≤105",
      "The sum of NNN across all tests won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "10\n3 3\n5 4\n7 4\n8 10\n9 16\n10 19\n10 20\n30 40\n100 120\n1000 1000",
        "output": "4\n48\n1440\n22560\n80640\n725760\n0\n422027771\n488057398\n656420449",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The valid permutations are [1,2,3],[3,1,2],[2,1,3],[3,2,1][1,2,3], [3,1,2], [2,1,3], [3,2,1][1,2,3],[3,1,2],[2,1,3],[3,2,1].\nTest case 666: There are no valid permutations."
      }
    ]
